// Fixture: init_gap_persists_across_4gen_chain
// Rule under test: GDDL Spec v4 §12 phase 8 -- extends
// init_uninitialized_only_caught_at_export.gddl's 2-instance chain to FOUR
// generations, none of them `delete`-marked. Confirms a gap introduced at generation 1
// and never touched by ANY descendant is still caught -- not silently accepted or
// "forgotten" partway through a longer chain than what's been tested so far. Per the
// already-established independent-per-instance phase-8 rule (confirmed earlier this
// project: phase 8 checks each non-`delete` instance's own finished tree
// independently, no cross-instance blocking/cascading), every one of the four
// instances here should be reported, not just the last.

define Stats
	hp = u32
	mp = u32

Stats Gen1
	hp = 100
	// mp: never touched, starting right here at generation 1.

Stats Gen2 = Gen1
	hp = 110
	// mp: still never touched.

Stats Gen3 = Gen2
	hp = 120
	// mp: still never touched.

Stats Gen4 = Gen3
	hp = 130
	// mp: still never touched, four generations deep from where the gap started.

// Expected (prediction, pending golden output from Compiler Core reference run):
//   All four instances (Gen1, Gen2, Gen3, Gen4) independently fail phase 8: missing
//   field `mp` in each, none of them `delete`-marked so none are exempt. Four separate
//   errors, not one root-caused error with three "blocked" markers (per the
//   already-confirmed phase-8-doesn't-cascade rule) and not a gap that gets silently
//   dropped partway through the chain.
